06202.eml,"> Le 22-mai-10 =E0 17:36, Mike Swingler a =E9crit :
>=20
>>> I don't think this was mentioned but the Mac beta of the Chrome =
browser will now run applets which I gather is dependent on this java =
upgrade.
>>>=20
>>> (Not that I am in any way suggesting Mac users should use anything =
other than Safari themselves, but if one produces web sites that contain =
Java applets it is obviously something which one has to be aware of.)
>>=20
>> This is because the out-of-process Plugin2 is now present in =
/Library/Internet Plug-Ins by default, and is picked up automatically by =
browsers that support it.
>=20
> Which browsers is that?
> My java preferences indicate I wish JDK 1.6 but browserspy confirms =
I'm running 1.5:
> 	http://browserspy.dk/java.php
> (for Safari and Camino at least)

Off the top of my head:

Safari will pickup Plugin2 if Plugin1 is not present - which Java =
Preferences toggles
Chrome picks up Plugin2 only
Firefox is hardwired to Plugin1 with the JEP/MRJ, unless you remove it =
them from (app)/Contents/MacOS/plugins
Camino is also hardwired with the JEP/MRJ, but does not pick up Plugin2 =
if they are disabled (not sure why)
Opera seems to always die on launch for me

Regards,
Mike Swingler
Java Runtime Engineer
Apple Inc.

