<a name=""When:4:23:56PM""><a href=""http://www.salon.com/tech/feature/2002/07/30/file_trading/print.html"">Salon</a>: ""Listen's $10-per-month Rhapsody service has a fantastic interface, and, since it has content from all five labels, you can find much of what you'd like on it. You can listen to any song as often as you'd like -- an option that gives a taste of what a perfect subscription service would feel like. The only trouble is, Listen won't let you burn -- and, as one file trader asked, 'Who wants to be stuck listening to shit at their computer?'"" &nbsp;<a href=""http://scriptingnews.userland.com/backissues/2002/07/30#When:4:23:56PM"" title=""Permanent link to this item in archive.""><img src=""http://www.scripting.com/images/2001/09/20/sharpPermaLink3.gif"" height=""9"" width=""6"" border=""0""></a><br><br>
