			<img src=""http://home.cnet.com/b.gif"" width=""10"" height=""1"" border=""0"">
			<font face=""Arial, Helvetica"" size=""-2"">July 11, 2002</font><br>
			<img src=""http://home.cnet.com/b.gif"" width=""1"" height=""3""><br>
			<table cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 width=412>
            	<tr valign=top><td width=90 align=right>
                	<img src=""http://a.r.tv.com/cnet.1d/i/nl/ce/cg/colind.gif"" width=""66"" height=""86"" border=""0""><br>
                    <font face=""arial, helvetica"" size=""-2"" color=""#666666"">
                     --Colin Duwe<br>
                     Associate Editor<br>
                     CNET Electronics<br></font>
                 	 </td><td width=10></td>
                     <td><font face=""Arial, Helvetica"">
                         <font color=""#333333""><B>Dear readers,</B></font><BR>
                         <font size=""-1"">
If the majority of your photos are posed snapshots and
landscapes, a fast camera may not matter. But if you've ever
missed a shot because your camera was busy processing the
previous photo, the Leica Digilux 1 will appeal to you. We liked
it too, and we gave it an Editors' Choice award.<!-- 
<br><a href=""http://clickthru.online.com/Click?q=48-ggFbIdBsy9_qy3wXl_kj2ZBSJu4R"" ><b>Read the full story</a> | <a href=""http://clickthru.online.com/Click?q=5d-JN-bIK0sj9xFgwDobvZm5yGKIaeR"" >Check prices</a> --></b></font>
