<!--STORY 1-->
 


<font size=""+1""><b>Desperately seeking chief ethics officer</b></a></font><br>

<b>Greedy CEOs</b> are making a bad name for the profession--and corporate America. The title chief executive officer now
conjures up an image of someone with questionable ethics, a
greedy disposition, and a disregard for shareholders. If
government-proposed remedies can""t adequately address this
<b>ethics crisis</b>, disgruntled shareholders surely will.


<br><img src=""http://www.zdnet.com/techupdate/i/arrow_blue.gif"" width=""8"" height=""10"" border=""0"">
