<b>Also: Ellison shrugs a No. 2 exec</b></a>


<P>

<!-- STORY 3 -->


   
<font size=""+1""><b>Standards stalled over royalty disputes</b></a></font><br>


The <b>World Wide Web Consortium</b> is bracing for a vote next week that could decide once and for all how the standards body will handle patented technology that comes with royalties attached. If patented technology is rejected, the vote could mark a major shift in the Internet standards battle. Major intellectual property holders such as <b>Microsoft</b> and <b>IBM</b> have a lot at stake.
 


<br><img src=""http://www.zdnet.com/techupdate/i/arrow_blue.gif"" width=""8"" height=""10"" border=""0"">
