<b>Read more survey results</b></a>





<p>



<!--STORY 5-->



<font size=""+1""><b>Oh look, a new bug in Outlook and IE</b></a></font><br>

A Danish security expert has warned of a security flaw in <b>Microsoft's ActiveX</b> scripting component that allows network attackers to peek at cookies, read files and even run programs on a victim's PC. The expert recommended that users disable ActiveX in IE and Outlook, at least until Microsoft releases a patch.

