<font size=3><b><a href=""http://clickthru.online.com/Click?q=d1-ulOzQpErJt-obd110-kl0aSxkZlR"" >Banc of America Securities begins coverage of Power Integrations with a ""market performer"" rating in tech notes 7/16/02 </a></b></font><br>
Analyst Douglas Lee says the maker of power supply integrated circuits is building a market niche with a more efficient and reliable technology than traditional approaches to converting AC-to-DC power supplies. He also notes Power Integrations is expanding its market with DC-to-DC power supply products, and says the firm's growth is based on converting today's power supplies to its more efficient technologies. As a result, the company doesn't need a boost in end-market demand to grow, Lee says. Although he sees a large, untapped market for Power Integrations and likes its long-term prospects, Lee suggests the stock is fairly valued. He believes shares of POWI are unlikely to rise much in the short term.<br><B>POWER INTEGRATIONS 18.72 5.23% </B><br>
